    "background_story": "Adeline was a French entomologist with a passion for silkworms, specifically the Bombyx mori species. Growing up in the countryside, she was fascinated by the intricate process of sericulture, where silkworms spun golden threads. Adeline dedicated her life to studying these creatures, traveling to Asia to learn from master sericulturists. She established a silk farm in her hometown, where she cultivated Bombyx mori and experimented with new breeding techniques. Her research led to breakthroughs in silk production, making it more sustainable and eco-friendly. Adeline's love for Bombyx mori took her on a journey of discovery, innovation, and entrepreneurship, earning her the nickname 'La Reine de la Soie' (The Silk Queen) among her peers.",
